1
00:05:07,058 --> 00:05:13,058
Searching for Cannibal Holocaust is a documentary
film directed by Calum Waddell.

2
00:10:14,117 --> 00:10:20,117
Italian horror fan and academic Calum Waddell speaks with some of the original makers of the controversial horror classic "Cannibal Holocaust" before
venturing into the Amazon jungle and surrounding city port, Leticia, to uncover some of the local stories behind the making of the motion picture.

3
00:15:21,176 --> 00:15:27,176
What is uncovered, however, leads to a wider and unexpected "true crime" story.

4
00:20:28,235 --> 00:20:34,235
Self, played by Calum Waddell.

5
00:25:35,294 --> 00:25:41,294
Self, played by Carl Gabriel Yorke.

6
00:30:42,352 --> 00:30:48,352
Self, played by Danilo Abadia.

7
00:35:49,411 --> 00:35:55,411
Self, played by Madame Blanca.

8
00:40:56,470 --> 00:41:02,470
Self, played by Ronaldo Blanca.

9
00:46:03,529 --> 00:46:09,529
Self, played by Tara Chowning.

10
00:51:10,588 --> 00:51:16,588
Slave of the Cannibal God (Italian title: La montagna del dio cannibale, literally The Mountain of the Cannibal God) is a 1978
Italian horror film starring Ursula Andress and Stacy Keach, with English dialogue, that was filmed in Sri Lanka.

11
00:56:17,647 --> 00:56:23,647
The film was also widely released in the U.S.

12
01:01:24,705 --> 01:01:30,705
in 1979 by New Line Cinema, and released in the U.K.

13
01:06:31,764 --> 01:06:37,764
under the title Prisoner of the Cannibal God, with
a poster designed by Sam Peffer.

14
01:11:38,823 --> 01:11:44,823
The film was banned in the U.K.

15
01:16:45,882 --> 01:16:51,882
until 2001 for its graphic violence and considered a "video nasty."

16
01:21:52,941 --> 01:21:58,941
The film explores themes of filmmaking, making of, amazon tribe.
